Pushed as Gerrit change 3068: commit 8274c1be6a2 on origin/main dcb35ce77fe.

The first `make verify` found 1 more test that encoded S7's single attempt: `tests/unit/reconciler/apply/test_applier_stale_binding_404.py::test_non_404_http_error_still_propagates`, where a 500 on every call through `applier.apply` expected 1 call and no sleep. It now asserts:
- 3 calls;
- 2 recorded `time.sleep` backoffs, in `[2, 3)` s and `[4, 5)` s;
- the raw 500 propagates.

It is added to file impact, which now has 10 paths and matches the diff. The plan text was corrected in 2 places and re-reviewed (PASS):
- the Retry-After path: `_run_atomic_op` passes `provider_delay_ms` to `attempt_retry`, and `plan_next_retry` takes `max(floor, provider)` and defers past the 15 s cap;
- `parse_retry_after` returns float seconds, or `None`.

`make verify` on the amended commit exited 0 (19708 passed, 86 skipped). Log: `.rebar/scratch/lane-ebf5/rt/verify2.log` in the epic worktree.
